event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":90,"item_id":"rs_0fad3f6edbdc4c67016aca81020b348193ac4b5ae955fb1143","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Examining concurrency in tests**\n\nI’m considering a concurrency issue related to using object assignment. It seems that I need to ensure tests are not just extensive but also well-structured. I can only write to a new file and cannot append; I'll explore using a unique suffix to differentiate edits. There’s also the idea of migrating the schema while maintaining priorities. Maybe I could add a new test by inserting it just before the last existing one; that sounds easier."}

